Keep the cleanup landing pad in eh_trampoline when the compiler optimizes. Its only purpose is
to make the personality routine run so objcxx_eh.cc can measure __cxa_exception, and at -O1 and
above clang drops the call to the empty destructor along with the landing pad. The size is then
never found and C++ exceptions thrown through Objective-C corrupt the heap.

--- a/eh_trampoline.cc
+++ b/eh_trampoline.cc
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 __attribute((visibility("hidden")))
 int eh_trampoline()
 {
-	struct X { ~X() {} } x;
+	struct X { ~X() { __asm__ volatile(""); } } x;
 	cxx_throw();
 	return 0;
 }
